        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కథకుడు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కథకుడు — kathakuḍu — \"a storyteller; a narrator\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కథకుడు పిల్లలకు ఒక వింత కథ చెప్పాడు. kathakuḍu pillalaku oka vinta katha ceppāḍu. The storyteller told the children a strange story."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కథ, a story, with -కుడు: one who tells it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కథకుడు (kathakuḍu) is borrowed from Sanskrit kathaka, \"a narrator, one who recites a story\" (Monier-Williams), built on kath, \"to tell\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
